G3918.b:
⟪πάρ-ειμι⟫,
[in LXX for ⁨בּוֹא⁩, etc.;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to be by⟫, ⟪at hand⟫ or ⟪present⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ of persons: ⟦Revelation 17:8|Re 17:8⟧; παρών (opp. to ἀπών), ⟦1 Corinthians 5:3|I Co 5:3⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 10:2|II Co 10:2⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 10:11|11⟧ ⟦2 Corinthians 13:2|13:2⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 13:10|10⟧; seq. ἐπί, c. gen., ⟦Acts 24:19|Ac 24:19⟧; ἐνώπιον, ⟦Acts 10:33|Ac 10:33⟧; ἐνθάδε, ⟦Acts 17:6|Ac 17:6⟧; πρός, c. acc. pers., ⟦Acts 12:20|Ac 12:20⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 11:8|II Co 11:8⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:18|Ga 4:18⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:20|20⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of things: of time, ὁ καιρός, ⟦John 7:6|Jo 7:6⟧; τ. παρόν, ⟦Hebrews 12:11|He 12:11⟧; ἡ ἀλήθεια, ⟦2 Peter 1:12|II Pe 1:12⟧; ταῦτα, ⟦2 Peter 1:9|II Pe 1:9⟧; τ. παρόντα, ⟦Hebrews 13:5|He 13:5⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to have come⟫ or ⟪arrived⟫ (Hdt., Thuc., al.; v. Field, Notes, 65): ⟦Luke 13:1|Lk 13:1⟧, ⟦John 11:28|Jo 11:28⟧, ⟦Acts 10:21|Ac 10:21⟧; seq. εἰς, ⟦Colossians 1:6|Col 1:6⟧; seq. ἐπί, c. acc. rei, ⟦Matthew 26:50|Mt 26:50⟧ (cf. συν-πάρειμι).†

G3925.b:
⟪παρ-εμ-βολή⟫, -ῆς, ἡ
(< παρεμβάλλω), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨מַחֲנֶה⁩;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪an insertion⟫, ⟪interpolation⟫ (Æschin.).
⟪2.⟫ In the Macedonian dialect (Rutherford, NPhr., 473), as a military term;
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪an army in battle array⟫: ⟦Hebrews 11:34|He 11:34⟧ (cf. ⟦Exodus 14:19|Ex 14:19⟧, ⟦Exodus 14:20|20⟧, ⟦Judges 4:16|Jg 4:16⟧, al.; freq. in Polyb.);
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪a camp⟫ (⟦Exodus 29:14|Ex 29:14⟧, al.): ⟦Hebrews 13:11|He 13:11⟧, ⟦Hebrews 13:13|13⟧, ⟦Revelation 20:9|Re 20:9⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ ⟪barracks⟫, ⟪soldiers' quarters⟫: ⟦Acts 21:34|Ac 21:34⟧, ⟦Acts 21:37|37⟧ ⟦Acts 22:24|22:24⟧ ⟦Acts 23:10|23:10⟧, ⟦Acts 23:16|16⟧, ⟦Acts 23:32|32⟧ ⟦Acts 28:16|28:16⟧ (WH, txt., R, om.).†

G3928.b:
⟪παρ-έρχομαι⟫,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨עבר⁩;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to pass⟫, ⟪pass by⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ of persons: absol., ⟦Luke 18:37|Lk 18:37⟧; c. acc. pers., ⟦Mark 6:48|Mk 6:48⟧; c. acc. lot., ⟦Acts 16:8|Ac 16:8⟧; seq. διά, c. gen., ⟦Matthew 8:28|Mt 8:28⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of things: τ. ποτήριον, ⟦Matthew 26:39|Mt 26:39⟧ (ἀπ’ ἐμοῦ), ⟦Matthew 26:42|Mt 26:42⟧; of time, ⟦Matthew 14:15|Mt 14:15⟧, ⟦Mark 14:35|Mk 14:35⟧, ⟦Acts 27:9|Ac 27:9⟧, ⟦1 Peter 4:3|I Pe 4:3⟧. Metaph.,
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to pass away⟫, ⟪perish⟫: ⟦Matthew 5:18|Mt 5:18⟧ ⟦Matthew 24:34|24:34⟧, ⟦Matthew 24:35|35⟧, ⟦Mark 13:30|Mk 13:30⟧, ⟦Mark 13:31|31⟧, ⟦Luke 16:17|Lk 16:17⟧ ⟦Luke 21:32|21:32⟧, ⟦Luke 21:33|33⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 5:17|II Co 5:17⟧, ⟦James 1:10|Ja 1:10⟧, ⟦2 Peter 3:10|II Pe 3:10⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to pass by⟫, ⟪neglect⟫, ⟪disregard⟫: c. acc. rei, ⟦Luke 11:42|Lk 11:42⟧ ⟦Luke 15:29|15:29⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to come to⟫, ⟪arrive⟫: ⟦Luke 12:37|Lk 12:37⟧ ⟦Luke 17:7|17:7⟧, ⟦Acts 24:7|Ac 24:7⟧, R, mg. (cf. ἀντι-παρέρχομαι).†
SYN.: παραβαίνω.

G3958.b:
⟪πάσχω⟫,
[in LXX: ⟦Amos 6:6|Am 6:6⟧ (⁨חלה⁩ ni.), Wi 12:27, Si 38:16, al.;] ⟪to suffer⟫, ⟪be acted on⟫, as opp. to acting, often limited by a word expressive of good or evil;
⟪(a)⟫ of misfortunes (most freq. without any limiting word): absol., ⟦Luke 22:15|Lk 22:15⟧ ⟦Luke 24:46|24:46⟧, ⟦Acts 1:3|Ac 1:3⟧ ⟦Acts 3:18|3:18⟧ ⟦Acts 17:3|17:3⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:26|I Co 12:26⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:18|He 2:18⟧ ⟦Hebrews 9:26|9:26⟧ ⟦Hebrews 13:12|13:12⟧, ⟦1 Peter 2:19|I Pe 2:19⟧, ⟦1 Peter 2:20|20⟧, ⟦1 Peter 2:23|23⟧ ⟦1 Peter 3:17|3:17⟧ ⟦1 Peter 4:15|4:15⟧, ⟦1 Peter 4:19|19⟧; seq. ὑπό, c. gen., ⟦Matthew 17:12|Mt 17:12⟧; ὑπέρ, ⟦Acts 9:16|Ac 9:16⟧, ⟦Philippians 1:20|Phl 1:20⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 1:5|II Th 1:5⟧, ⟦1 Peter 2:21|I Pe 2:21⟧; c. dat. ref., ⟦1 Peter 4:1|I Pe 4:1⟧; περί, c. gen. (seq. ὑπέρ), ⟦1 Peter 3:18|I Pe 3:18⟧; διά, c. acc., ⟦1 Peter 3:14|I Pe 3:14⟧; ὀλίγον (a little while), ⟦1 Peter 5:10|I Pe 5:10⟧; c. acc., ⟦Matthew 27:19|Mt 27:19⟧, ⟦Mark 9:12|Mk 9:12⟧, ⟦Luke 13:2|Lk 13:2⟧ ⟦Luke 24:26|24:26⟧, ⟦Acts 28:5|Ac 28:5⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 1:12|II Ti 1:12⟧, ⟦Hebrews 5:8|He 5:8⟧, ⟦Revelation 2:10|Re 2:10⟧; παθήματα, ⟦2 Corinthians 1:6|II Co 1:6⟧; ταῦτα, ⟦Galatians 3:4|Ga 3:4⟧ (EV; cf. Lft., in l., but v. infr.); acc. seq. ἀπό, ⟦Matthew 16:21|Mt 16:21⟧, ⟦Luke 9:22|Lk 9:22⟧ ⟦Luke 17:25|17:25⟧; ὑπό, ⟦Mark 5:26|Mk 5:26⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:14|I Th 2:14⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of pleasant experiences (but always with qualifying word, εὖ or acc. rei) : ⟦Galatians 3:4|Ga 3:4⟧ (cf. Grimm-Thayer, s.v.; Interp. Com., in l., but v. supr.) (cf. προ-, συν-πάσχω).†

G3962.b:
⟪πατήρ⟫, πατρός, -τρί, τέρα,
[in LXX chiefly and very freq. for ⁨אָב⁩;] ⟪a father⟫;
⟪1.⟫ prop.,
	⟪(a)⟫ of the male parent: ⟦Matthew 2:22|Mt 2:22⟧, ⟦Luke 1:17|Lk 1:17⟧, ⟦John 4:53|Jo 4:53⟧; anarth., ⟦Hebrews 12:7|He 12:7⟧ (M, Pr., 82 f.); pl., of both parents (cl.), ⟦Hebrews 11:23|He 11:23⟧; οἱ π. τ. σαρκός, ⟦Hebrews 12:9|He 12:9⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of a forefather or ancestor (in cl. usually in pl.; Hom., al.): ⟦Matthew 3:9|Mt 3:9⟧, ⟦Luke 1:73|Lk 1:73⟧, ⟦John 8:39|Jo 8:39⟧, al.; pl., ⟦Matthew 23:30|Mt 23:30⟧, ⟦Matthew 23:32|32⟧, ⟦Luke 6:23|Lk 6:23⟧, ⟦Luke 6:26|26⟧, ⟦John 4:20|Jo 4:20⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:1|I Co 10:1⟧, al.
⟪2.⟫ Metaph.,
	⟪(a)⟫ of an author, originator, or archetype (= αἴτιος, ἀρχηγός, etc.; Pind., Plat., al.): ⟦John 8:41|Jo 8:41-44⟧, ⟦Romans 4:11|Ro 4:11⟧, ⟦Romans 4:12|12⟧, ⟦Romans 4:16|16⟧.
	⟪(b)⟫ as a title of respect or honour, used of seniors, teachers and others in a position of responsible authority (⟦Judges 17:10|Jg 17:10⟧, ⟦2 Samuel 2:12|II Ki 2:12⟧, ⟦Proverbs 1:8|Pr 1:8⟧, al.): ⟦Matthew 23:9|Mt 23:9⟧, ⟦Acts 7:2|Ac 7:2⟧ ⟦Acts 22:1|22:1⟧, ⟦1 John 2:13|I Jo 2:13⟧.
⟪3.⟫ Of God (as in cl. of Zeus) as Father;
	⟪(a)⟫ of created things: τ. φώτων, ⟦James 1:17|Ja 1:17⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of all sentient beings: ⟦Ephesians 3:14|Eph 3:14⟧, ⟦Ephesians 3:15|15⟧, ⟦Hebrews 12:9|He 12:9⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ of men, esp. those in covenant relation with Him (freq in OT and later Jewish lit.; v. Dalman, Words, 184 ff.): ⟦Matthew 6:4|Mt 6:4⟧, ⟦Luke 6:36|Lk 6:36⟧, ⟦John 4:21|Jo 4:21⟧, ⟦James 3:9|Ja 3:9⟧, al.; ὁ π. ὁ ἐν (τ.) οὐρανοῖς, ⟦Matthew 5:16|Mt 5:16⟧, ⟦Mark 11:25|Mk 11:25⟧; ὁ π. ὁ οὐράνιος, ⟦Matthew 6:14|Mt 6:14⟧ ⟦Matthew 15:13|15:13⟧; esp. in the Epp., of Christians: ⟦Romans 8:15|Ro 8:15⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 6:18|II Co 6:18⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:6|Ga 4:6⟧, ⟦Ephesians 2:18|Eph 2:18⟧ ⟦Ephesians 4:6|4:6⟧, ⟦1 John 2:1|I Jo 2:1⟧; c. gen. qual., τ. οἰκτιρμῶν, ⟦2 Corinthians 1:3|II Co 1:3⟧; τ. δοξῆς, ⟦Ephesians 1:17|Eph 1:17⟧;
	⟪(d)⟫ of Christ (Dalman, Words, 190 ff.);
		⟪(α)⟫ by our Lord himself: ὁ π., ⟦Matthew 11:25|Mt 11:25-27⟧, ⟦Luke 10:21|Lk 10:21⟧, ⟦Luke 10:22|22⟧, ⟦John 5:20|Jo 5:20-23⟧, al.; ὁ π. μου, ⟦Matthew 11:27|Mt 11:27⟧, al.; ὁ ἐν τ. οὐρανοῖς, ⟦Matthew 7:11|Mt 7:11⟧, al.; ὁ οὐράνιος, ⟦Matthew 15:13|Mt 15:13⟧; vocat., ⟦John 11:41|Jo 11:41⟧ ⟦John 12:27|12:27⟧, ⟦John 12:28|28⟧ ⟦John 17:1|17:1⟧, ⟦John 17:5|5⟧, ⟦John 17:11|11⟧, ⟦John 17:20|20⟧, ⟦John 17:25|25⟧ (cf. Abbott, JG., 96 f.);
		⟪(β)⟫ by Apostles: ⟦John 1:14|Jo 1:14⟧ (anarth.; v. M, Pr., 82 f.), ⟦Romans 15:6|Ro 15:6⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 1:3|II Co 1:3⟧ ⟦2 Corinthians 11:31|11:31⟧, ⟦Ephesians 1:3|Eph 1:3⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:3|Col 1:3⟧, ⟦Hebrews 1:5|He 1:5⟧, ⟦1 Peter 1:3|I Pe 1:3⟧, ⟦Revelation 1:6|Re 1:6⟧ (cf. Westc., Epp. Jo., 27-34).

G3985.b:
⟪πειράζω⟫, poët. and late prose form of πειράω, q.v.,
[in LXX for ⁨נסה⁩ pi.;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to make proof of⟫ (Hom.).
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to try⟫, ⟪attempt⟫ (Luc., Polyb., al.): c. inf. (v. M, Pr., 205; Bl., § 69, 4), ⟦Acts 9:26|Ac 9:26⟧ ⟦Acts 16:7|16:7⟧ ⟦Acts 24:6|24:6⟧.
⟪3.⟫ In LXX and NT, like Heb. ⁨נסה⁩, c. acc. pers., ⟪to test⟫, ⟪try⟫, ⟪prove⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ in a good sense: ⟦John 6:6|Jo 6:6⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 13:5|II Co 13:5⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:17|He 11:17⟧, ⟦Revelation 2:2|Re 2:2⟧; esp. of trials and afflictions sent or permitted by God (⟦Genesis 22:1|Ge 22:1⟧, ⟦Exodus 20:20|Ex 20:20⟧, Wi 3:5, al.), ⟦1 Corinthians 10:13|I Co 10:13⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:18|He 2:18⟧ ⟦Hebrews 4:15|4:15⟧ ⟦Hebrews 11:17|11:17⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:37|37⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:10|Re 3:10⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ in a bad sense (Apoll. Rhod., 3, 10): of the attempts made to ensnare Jesus in his speech, ⟦Matthew 16:1|Mt 16:1⟧ ⟦Matthew 19:3|19:3⟧ ⟦Matthew 22:18|22:18⟧, ⟦Matthew 22:35|35⟧, ⟦Mark 8:11|Mk 8:11⟧ ⟦Mark 10:2|10:2⟧ ⟦Mark 12:15|12:15⟧, ⟦Luke 11:16|Lk 11:16⟧, ⟦John 8:6|Jo 8:[6]⟧; of temptation to sin, ⟪to tempt⟫, ⟦James 1:13|Ja 1:13⟧, ⟦James 1:14|14⟧ (v. Hort, in l.), ⟦Galatians 6:1|Ga 6:1⟧, ⟦Revelation 2:10|Re 2:10⟧; esp. of temptations of the devil, ⟦Matthew 4:1|Mt 4:1⟧, ⟦Matthew 4:3|3⟧, ⟦Mark 1:13|Mk 1:13⟧, ⟦Luke 4:2|Lk 4:2⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:5|I Co 7:5⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:5|I Th 3:5⟧; ὁ πειράζων, ⟪the tempter⟫, ⟦Matthew 4:3|Mt 4:3⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:5|I Th 3:5⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ in bad sense also (⟦Exodus 17:2|Ex 17:2⟧, ⟦Exodus 17:7|7⟧, ⟦Numbers 14:22|Nu 14:22⟧, al.), of distrustful testing, trying or challenging of God: ⟦Acts 15:10|Ac 15:10⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:9|I Co 10:9⟧ (WH, mg., ἐξεπείρασαν), ⟦Hebrews 3:9|He 3:9⟧; τ. πνεῦμα Κυρίου, ⟦Acts 5:9|Ac 5:9⟧ (cf. ἐκ-πειράζω).†
SYN.: δοκιμάζω, q.v.

G3986.b:
† ⟪πειρασμός⟫, -οῦ, ὁ
(< πειράζω), [in LXX for ⁨מַסָּה⁩, ⁨עִנְיָן⁩;]
⟪1.⟫ = πεῖρα, ⟪an experiment⟫ (Diosc.).
⟪2.⟫ ⟪a trial⟫, of ethical purpose and effect, whether good or evil (v. Hort on ⟦James 1:13|Ja 1:13⟧);
	⟪(a)⟫ in good or neutral sense: ⟦Galatians 4:14|Ga 4:14⟧, ⟦James 1:12|Ja 1:12⟧, ⟦1 Peter 4:12|I Pe 4:12⟧; esp. of afflictions sent by God (⟦Deuteronomy 7:19|De 7:19⟧, Si 2:1, al.): ⟦2 Peter 2:9|II Pe 2:9⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:10|Re 3:10⟧; pl., ⟦Luke 22:28|Lk 22:28⟧, ⟦Acts 20:19|Ac 20:19⟧, ⟦James 1:2|Ja 1:2⟧, ⟦1 Peter 1:6|I Pe 1:6⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of trial regarded as leading to sin, ⟪temptation⟫: ⟦Luke 8:13|Lk 8:13⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:13|I Co 10:13⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 6:9|I Ti 6:9⟧; of the temptation of Jesus by the devil, ⟦Luke 4:13|Lk 4:13⟧; εἰσφέρειν (ἔρχεσθαι, εἰσέρχ-) εἰς π., ⟦Matthew 6:13|Mt 6:13⟧ ⟦Matthew 26:41|26:41⟧, ⟦Mark 14:38|Mk 14:38⟧, ⟦Luke 11:4|Lk 11:4⟧ ⟦Luke 22:40|22:40⟧, ⟦Luke 22:46|46⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ of the testing or challenge of God by man (v.s. πειράζω, 3, c.): ⟦Hebrews 3:8|He 3:8⟧ (LXX: ⟦Psalms 95:9|Ps 94 (95):9⟧, where κατὰ τ. ἡμέραν πειρασμοῦ = ⁨מַסָּה⁩ ⁨כְּיוֹם⁩ ⟪as the day of Massah⟫).†
SYN.: δοκίμιον.

G3992.b:
⟪πέμπω⟫,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨שׁלח⁩;] ⟪to send⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of persons: c. acc., absol., ⟦Matthew 22:7|Mt 22:7⟧, ⟦Luke 7:19|Lk 7:19⟧, ⟦John 1:22|Jo 1:22⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 9:3|II Co 9:3⟧, al.; ptcp. seq. verb., ⟦Matthew 14:10|Mt 14:10⟧, ⟦Acts 19:31|Ac 19:31⟧, al.; ptcp. seq. διά (= Heb. ⁨בְּיוֹד⁩probably misspelled בְּיַד, ⟦1 Samuel 16:20|I Ki 16:20⟧, al.), ⟦Matthew 11:2|Mt 11:2⟧ (cf. ⟦Revelation 1:1|Re 1:1⟧); of teachers sent by God, ⟦John 1:33|Jo 1:33⟧ ⟦John 4:34|4:34⟧, ⟦Romans 8:3|Ro 8:3⟧, al.; c. acc. et dat., ⟦1 Corinthians 4:17|I Co 4:17⟧, ⟦Philippians 2:19|Phl 2:19⟧; seq. πρός, c. acc., ⟦Luke 4:26|Lk 4:26⟧, ⟦John 16:7|Jo 16:7⟧, al.; seq. λέγων (cf. Heb. ⁨שָׁלַח⁩ ⁨לֵאמֹר⁩ ⟦Genesis 38:25|Ge 38:25⟧, al.), ⟦Luke 7:6|Lk 7:6⟧, ⟦Luke 7:19|19⟧; seq. εἰς, c. acc. loc., ⟦Matthew 2:8|Mt 2:8⟧, ⟦Luke 15:15|Lk 15:15⟧, al.; seq. εἰς (of purpose), ⟦Ephesians 6:22|Eph 6:22⟧, ⟦Colossians 4:8|Col 4:8⟧, ⟦1 Peter 2:14|I Pe 2:14⟧; c. inf., ⟦John 1:33|Jo 1:33⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 16:3|I Co 16:3⟧, ⟦Revelation 22:16|Re 22:16⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of things: ⟦Revelation 11:10|Re 11:10⟧; seq. εἰς, ⟦Revelation 1:11|Re 1:11⟧; id., of purpose, ⟦Acts 11:29|Ac 11:29⟧, ⟦Philippians 4:16|Phl 4:16⟧; c. dat. pers., ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:11|II Th 2:11⟧; π. τ. δρέπανον σου (cf. εξαποστείλατε δρέπανα = ⁨שָׁלַח⁩ ⁨מַגָּל⁩, ⟦Joel 3:13|Jl 3 (4):13⟧), ⟦Revelation 14:15|Re 14:15⟧, ⟦Revelation 14:18|18⟧ (cf. ἀνα-, ἐκ-, μετα-, προ-, συν-πέμπω).
SYN.: ἀποστέλλω, q.v.

G3996.b:
⟪πενθέω⟫, -ῶ,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨אבל⁩;] ⟪to mourn⟫ (⟪for⟫), ⟪lament⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ intrans. : ⟦Matthew 5:4|Mt 5:4⟧ (⟦Matthew 5:5|5⟧) ⟦Matthew 9:15|9:15⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 5:2|I Co 5:2⟧; π. καὶ κλαίειν, ⟦Matthew 16:10|Mt 16:10⟧, ⟦Luke 6:25|Lk 6:25⟧, ⟦James 4:9|Ja 4:9⟧, ⟦Revelation 18:15|Re 18:15⟧, ⟦Revelation 18:19|19⟧; seq. ἐπί, c. acc., ⟦Revelation 18:11|Re 18:11⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ trans., c. acc., ⟦2 Corinthians 12:21|II Co 12:21⟧.†
SYN.: v.s. θρηνέω.
